<title>NORWAY: Saga shares tumble on Santa Fe deal.</title>
<headline>Saga shares tumble on Santa Fe deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Norwegian oil company Saga Petroleum fell sharply on Wednesday after the company announced it had bought Kuwaiti-owned North Sea exploration group Santa Fe Exploration for $1.23 billion.</p>
<p>The shares, which had been suspended from trading on the Oslo bourse on Monday pending an announcement, resumed trading at 1044 GMT.</p>
<p>The A share fell nine crowns to a low at 96.50 crowns before climbing back to 100.50 at 1100 GMT.</p>
<p>Saga's Bs were down five crowns at 92 crowns after hitting a low at 88 crowns.</p>
<p>Saga bought Santa Fe from Kuwait Petroleum Corp.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
